-- Version 14 → 15: discussion forums.
--
-- The same dual-path story as 1.sqm and 2.sqm: a fresh volume runs `CREATE
-- TABLE` from Forums.sq and gets this for free; a volume already at version 14
-- — the deployed one — runs this instead. Without it the deployed database
-- would stay at the old shape and every forum query would die on `no such
-- table`. MigrationTest is the guarantee that this lands on exactly the schema
-- the .sq files declare; see its preamble.
--
-- Pure CREATE TABLE, so there is nothing to back-fill: a table that did not
-- exist has no rows, and "this project has no forums yet" is the correct state
-- for every project that predates the feature. Note that it is also the correct
-- state *afterwards* — unlike 4.sqm, which had to give existing projects the
-- board columns that ProjectRepository seeds into new ones, there is no forum
-- every project ought to have. A project with no forums shows an empty
-- Discussion tab, which is what a project nobody has set one up in should show.
--
-- The statement below is a verbatim copy of Forums.sq's CREATE TABLE block,
-- minus the prose — see that file for what each column and constraint is for,
-- and for the two things (per-forum access, history) it deliberately omits.

CREATE TABLE forums (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    project_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
    name TEXT NOT NULL COLLATE NOCASE,

    description TEXT,

    position INTEGER NOT NULL,

    created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,

    FOREIGN KEY (project_id) REFERENCES projects(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    UNIQUE (project_id, name)
);
